Chapter: GopTrack
  cites Works chapter GopTrackDb
  cites Data chapter Row
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites UI chapter Layout
  cites UI chapter Theme
  cites UI chapter DataTable

 The issue tracker's list view, moved out of `apps/guios/TrackerApp.codex`
 when the guios shell retired into GopDesk. The data layer moved with it
 as `GopTrackDb`, unchanged: it is a relational store over `DbServer` with
 no UI in it, which is why it survived the retirement while the four
 menu-item chapters did not.

 This is a real view over real rows. The issues are inserted into a
 catalog, queried back through the executor, filtered, and turned into
 table rows -- not a picture of a tracker.

 **What did NOT come across, and it is most of the old chapter.** The
 kanban board, the sprint-cycle dashboard, the detail overlay, the command
 palette and the focus ring were all built as `(GopBuf, ShellUiState)`
 painting through `gop-render-tree`, and every one of them needs UI state
 the shell owned. They are worth having and they are not lost -- the old
 chapter stays in the depot until they land -- but a pane that shows the
 issues is the rung that proves the data layer reaches the glass, and
 shipping the board half-wired would have proved less.

Section: Names

 Status and priority are stored as integers and rendered as words. The
 numbers are the database's and the words are this view's.

  gtk-status-name : Integer -> Text
  gtk-status-name (s) =
    if s == 0 then "Backlog"
    else if s == 1 then "Todo"
    else if s == 2 then "In Progress"
    else if s == 3 then "In Review"
    else if s == 4 then "Done"
    else "Cancelled"

  gtk-priority-name : Integer -> Text
  gtk-priority-name (p) =
    if p == 0 then "Urgent"
    else if p == 1 then "High"
    else if p == 2 then "Medium"
    else if p == 3 then "Low"
    else "None"

Section: Filter

 Three filters: everything, open only, done only. Open excludes both Done
 and Cancelled, because an abandoned issue is not outstanding work.

  gtk-filter-all : Integer = 0
  gtk-filter-open : Integer = 1
  gtk-filter-done : Integer = 2

  gtk-filter-name : Integer -> Text
  gtk-filter-name (f) =
    if f == gtk-filter-open then "open"
    else if f == gtk-filter-done then "done"
    else "all"

  gtk-filter-ok : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  gtk-filter-ok (filter) (status) =
    if filter == gtk-filter-all then True
    else if filter == gtk-filter-open then
      (if status == 4 then False else if status == 5 then False else True)
    else status == 4

Section: Table

 Column widths are in pixels and the compositor cuts a cell's text to its
 own column, so a width is a character budget: 8 pixels a character, less
 4 for the cell's left inset. These are sized to the widest value each
 column actually holds -- `CDX-142` is 7, `In Progress` is 11, `security`
 is 8 -- rather than to the header, which is what the inherited widths
 were sized to. At 54 pixels the ID column showed `CDX-14`.

  gtk-columns : List TableColumn
  gtk-columns = [
    table-column "key" "ID" 68,
    table-column "status" "Status" 100,
    table-column "title" "Title" 200,
    table-column "priority" "Priority" 68,
    table-column "label" "Label" 76,
    table-column "assignee" "Assignee" 76
  ]

  gtk-rows-from-db : List RowData, Integer, Integer, Integer, List TableRow -> List TableRow
  gtk-rows-from-db (rows) (filter) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let row = list-at rows i
    in let status = tk-row-int row "status"
    in if gtk-filter-ok filter status == False
    then gtk-rows-from-db rows filter (i + 1) n acc
    else let tr = table-row (show (i + 1)) [
        tk-row-text row "key",
        gtk-status-name status,
        tk-row-text row "title",
        gtk-priority-name (tk-row-int row "priority"),
        tk-row-text row "label",
        tk-row-text row "assignee"
      ]
    in gtk-rows-from-db rows filter (i + 1) n (list-push acc tr)

 The row id is the index in the UNFILTERED result, so a row keeps its
 identity when the filter changes.

  gtk-data-table : DbServer, Integer, Integer -> DataTableState
  gtk-data-table (srv) (filter) (sel) =
    let result = tk-db-all-issues srv
    in let rows = gtk-rows-from-db (result.qr-rows) filter 0 (result.qr-count) []
    in data-table-select-row (data-table-new "issues" gtk-columns rows) sel

Section: Tree

  gtk-tree : DbServer, Integer, Integer -> WidgetNode
  gtk-tree (srv) (filter) (sel) =
    let dt = gtk-data-table srv filter sel
    in let open-n = tk-db-count-open srv
    in let all-n = tk-db-issue-count srv
    in widget-panel "gtk-root" DirColumn 6 [
      widget-label "gtk-title" ("Issues -- " & show open-n & " open of " & show all-n & ", showing " & gtk-filter-name filter),
      widget-separator "gtk-sep",
      widget-set-flex (data-table-widget dt) 1,
      widget-separator "gtk-sep2",
      widget-label "gtk-help" "f cycles the filter   up/down select   Esc returns"
    ]
